  "prompt": "Can I still file the annual income tax return today?",
  "runtimeCommit": "ba08ae790021ac1e22f438a82372a643dd886de0",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, you can still file your annual income tax return today. The deadline for filing the annual income tax return in the Philippines is typically April 15 of the following year after the taxable year, but extensions may apply.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIf you are filing today and it is past the usual deadline, you may incur penalties for late filing unless you have a valid reason for the delay or have applied for an extension. It is advisable to check with the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) for any specific guidelines or relief measures that may apply to your situation.",
